/-!
# Transitivity of separable field extensions

Source: Stacks Project, Algebra, Tags 030U and 030W, combined by tensor reassociation
(blueprint: lem-sfb-separable-field-extension-transitivity).
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u v w

namespace Algebra

/-- Separability of possibly transcendental field extensions is transitive.
Source: Stacks Project, Algebra, Tags 030U and 030W
(blueprint: lem-sfb-separable-field-extension-transitivity).

Proof:
1. If `k` has characteristic zero, apply
   `lem-weil-pbc-char-zero-field-extension-separable` to `L/k`. Otherwise its characteristic
   is a prime `p`. Fix any extension field `E/k`. Tensor products below carry the ring
   structure of `lem-weil-pbc-algebra-tensor-pushout-universal-property`.
2. Put `R = K ⊗[k] E`. Write a nilpotent `x` as a finite sum of pure tensors
   `aᵢ ⊗ eᵢ`, using `def-weil-pbc-module-tensor-product`. The intermediate field
   `K₀ = k(a₁, ..., aᵣ)` is finitely generated, hence separably generated by `hK` and
   `def-weil-pbc-separable-field-extension`. Thus `K₀ ⊗[k] E` is reduced by
   `lem-weil-pbc-separably-generated-tensor-reduced`. Its canonical ring map into `R`
   is injective: `E` is flat by `lem-weil-pbc-module-over-field-flat`, and
   `lem-trf-flat-tensor-preserves-injection` applies after interchanging factors.
   The interchange sends `a ⊗ e` to `e ⊗ a`, with the reverse formula as inverse.
   The lift `x₀` of the displayed sum has zero power by this injectivity and the ring-map
   identity. Reducedness gives `x₀ = 0`, hence `x = 0`. Therefore `R` is reduced.
3. Similarly, for a nilpotent finite sum `y = ∑ bⱼ ⊗ rⱼ` in `L ⊗[K] R`, put
   `L₀ = K(b₁, ..., bₛ)`. By `hL` this field is separably generated over `K`.
   The same reduced-tensor lemma applies to the reduced `K`-algebra `R`, even though
   `R` need not be a field. Its flatness as a `K`-vector space makes the canonical
   ring map `L₀ ⊗[K] R → L ⊗[K] R` injective. The lift of `y` is nilpotent, hence zero.
   Therefore `L ⊗[K] R` is reduced.
4. The tensor universal properties give inverse ring maps
   `L ⊗[K] (K ⊗[k] E) → L ⊗[k] E` and in the other direction, given respectively by
   `b ⊗ (a ⊗ e) ↦ ba ⊗ e` and `b ⊗ e ↦ b ⊗ (1 ⊗ e)`.
   Additivity and balancing over both fields follow from the scalar tower; in particular
   `bc ⊗ (a ⊗ e)` and `b ⊗ (ca ⊗ e)` have the same image. Products and units are
   preserved on pure tensors. Both composites fix pure tensors, by balancing over `K`,
   so are identities. Thus `L ⊗[k] E` is reduced as well.
5. Since `E/k` was arbitrary, apply
   `lem-weil-pbc-geometrically-reduced-extension-separable` to `L/k` in characteristic
   `p`. Its conclusion is precisely `IsSeparableExtension k L`. No algebraicity,
   finiteness, finite generation or perfectness assumption was used.
-/
theorem isSeparableExtension_trans
    (k : Type u) (K : Type v) (L : Type w)
    [Field k] [Field K] [Field L]
    [Algebra k K] [Algebra K L] [Algebra k L] [IsScalarTower k K L]
    (hK : IsSeparableExtension k K) (hL : IsSeparableExtension K L) :
    IsSeparableExtension k L := by
  sorry

end Algebra
